openapi: 3.0.3
info:
  title: Splunk Enterprise Security — Set Finding Disposition (v1 incidents, HAR-verified)
  description: >
    Sets the review DISPOSITION on a Splunk Enterprise Security 8 FINDING via the
    Mission Control REST API — the exact call the Mission Control UI fires when an
    analyst changes the Disposition dropdown on a finding (captured from a browser
    HAR):
      POST /v1/incidents/{id}
      body: {"disposition": "disposition:NN", "inherit_fields": false}
    (The MC UI also appends ?notable_time=<epoch>, but the working standalone
    UpdateIncident plugin sets dispositions on this same endpoint WITHOUT it and
    still returns 200 — so this plugin omits the query param entirely to stay
    structurally identical to that working call.)
    Does NOT create a Mission Control investigation. Disposition ONLY — status and
    every other field are left unchanged.

    Self-authed plugin (its manifest carries its own Bearer token); intended to be
    pulled into an agent via RequiredSkillSets, NOT inlined as an agent SkillGroup.

    KEY: {id} is the FINDING ID, passed as the FULL composite string
    (GUID@@notable@@time<epoch>), a single value — NOT a bare GUID and NOT a JSON
    array. e.g. 8b7b3093-2f9c-4393-b8d6-9bd21580cad6@@notable@@time1786393748

    CONTENT-TYPE NOTE: the UI HAR labels the request
    application/x-www-form-urlencoded, but the body bytes (content-length 55) are
    exactly the JSON payload {"disposition":"disposition:15","inherit_fields":false}
    (55 bytes; a form-encoded body would be ~47-49) — i.e. a browser mislabel. The
    MC handler accepts JSON, and the working standalone UpdateIncident plugin
    confirmed application/json returns 200. This spec therefore sends
    application/json. If a live 415 ever appears, switch the requestBody content
    key to application/x-www-form-urlencoded.
  version: 1.1.0

servers:
  - url: https://es-dev-accenture.splunkcloud.com:8089/servicesNS/nobody/missioncontrol

paths:
  /v1/incidents/{id}:
    post:
      operationId: AddFindingDisposition
      summary: Set the disposition on an ES finding (HAR-verified UI call)
      description: |
        Sets the review disposition on an ES 8 finding, identified by {id}, WITHOUT
        opening a Mission Control investigation. This is the same review-update call
        the Mission Control UI fires when the Disposition dropdown is changed
        (HAR-verified): POST /v1/incidents/{id}?notable_time=<epoch>.

        PATH PARAMETER:
        - id: the FINDING ID (or investigation id/display_id). For a finding, this
          is the FULL composite exactly as received — GUID@@notable@@time<epoch> —
          passed as ONE string. Do NOT split it, do NOT strip the @@notable@@time
          segment, and do NOT wrap it in a JSON array.
          e.g. 8b7b3093-2f9c-4393-b8d6-9bd21580cad6@@notable@@time1786393748

        BODY (application/json):
        - disposition: the disposition CODE (REQUIRED), e.g. disposition:16 — the
          code from disposition_lookup, NEVER the human label. Security Copilot
          codes: disposition:16 (SC True Positive), disposition:15 (SC Benign
          Positive). Send disposition ONLY — do NOT send status, urgency,
          sensitivity, assignee, or any other field; status and all other fields
          are left unchanged.
        - inherit_fields: optional boolean; send false so a finding-level
          disposition does not propagate to a parent investigation. (Present in the
          UI HAR body.)

        #ExamplePrompts
        - AddFindingDisposition id 8b7b3093-...@@notable@@time1786393748 disposition disposition:16
        - Set the disposition of finding 8b7b3093-...@@notable@@time1786393748 to disposition:15
        - Mark this finding as Security Copilot True Positive (disposition:16).
      parameters:
        - name: id
          in: path
          required: true
          description: >
            The finding ID (full composite GUID@@notable@@time<epoch>) or an
            investigation id/display_id. Single string — never a JSON array.
          schema:
            type: string
            example: "8b7b3093-2f9c-4393-b8d6-9bd21580cad6@@notable@@time1786393748"
      requestBody:
        required: true
        description: The disposition to set (JSON body; see CONTENT-TYPE NOTE in info.description).
        content:
          application/json:
            schema:
              $ref: '#/components/schemas/SetDispositionPayload'
            example:
              disposition: "disposition:16"
              inherit_fields: false
      responses:
        '200':
          description: Disposition set. Returns the review record id.
          content:
            application/json:
              schema:
                $ref: '#/components/schemas/SetDispositionResponse'
        '400':
          description: Bad request (e.g. missing notable_time, missing disposition, or malformed id).
        '401':
          description: Unauthorized (token missing/invalid or insufficient MC capability).
        '404':
          description: Finding/investigation not found for the supplied id.

components:
  securitySchemes:
    bearerAuth:
      type: apiKey
      in: header
      name: Authorization
  security:
    - bearerAuth: []
  schemas:
    SetDispositionPayload:
      type: object
      required:
        - disposition
      properties:
        disposition:
          type: string
          description: >
            The disposition CODE from disposition_lookup (never the label), e.g.
            disposition:16. Security Copilot codes: disposition:16 (SC True
            Positive), disposition:15 (SC Benign Positive).
          example: "disposition:16"
        inherit_fields:
          type: boolean
          description: >
            Optional. Send false so a finding-level disposition change does not
            propagate to a parent investigation.
          example: false
    SetDispositionResponse:
      type: object
      properties:
        id:
          type: string
          description: The ID of the review/update record created.
          example: "d086c7f1-2b4f-439a-a1ca-a775bf572d74"
